{
  "_comment": "The route limit covers the pre-join entrance (#712); SpaceCall loads the admitted call after Join (#730), and builds its join client from the generated ChalkPublicApi (only the unauthenticated /v1/public operations), so the MCP OAuth contract (#814) stays out of the route. The route measures about 205.5 KiB and its ceiling is 217 KiB, down from 219. Five fresh-context bundle-only runs per revision on Linux x64, 8-core Intel Xeon, Node 24.19.0, pnpm 12.8.1 and Chromium 151.0.7922.34 give non-board JavaScript gzip min/median/max of 386.486/386.486/386.486 KiB on master 35a9d072c and 386.560/386.560/386.560 KiB with send recovery. Validating the call path with Effect Schema instead of zod, which also removes zod and its English locale from the call JavaScript, cut 2.1 KiB (386.5 to 384.5 KiB on the same machine), so the non-board ceiling went down from 387 to 385 KiB. Board, CSS, timing, video-quality and leak limits and the historical timing baseline remain unchanged. The route limit alone falls, from 219 to 217 KiB. The route CSS ceiling is 28 KiB: it rose from 32 to 33 for the transcript language picker (#880) and fell to 28 in #919. The action.* limits moved here unchanged from the latency kit's own budget file. Proposed from 40 kept cycles per plane on staging: one headless and one headed Chromium run from a 4 vCPU droplet in DigitalOcean sgp1 on 7 Nov 2026. Each p95Ms is 1.5 times the larger of the two runs' p95, rounded up to 50 ms. A limit that differs by media plane is keyed by the plane first, for example chalk_sfu.action.leave_ms; they warn until seven nightly values of that plane stay within tolerancePct. The SFU loopback and impairment tests are deterministic, so their pass rates must stay at 1 and gate from the start. proof.leave_median_ms starts as a warning at the Leave proof's own 5000 ms ceiling on the slowest leave. Real-node budgets (sfu.*, nightly action.*, proof.*, device.*) set gate to true only in a budgets pull request that cites seven nightly values with a run-to-run spread below tolerancePct.",
